From cc4f097cf93388e3b3bf82bb5563b1a88d3c40ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:48:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shell: Always-on display while the panel dozes

With the setting org.plinius.display always-on-display, the built-in
panel no longer goes off when the screen blanks: it dozes in the OLED's
low-power mode (phoc-plinius' power mode "doze") and shows a black
overlay with the time, the date, the battery and an icon per app with
notifications. Not during calls, the proximity sensor blanks the screen
then; a call that starts while dozing switches the panel off.

For the shell a dozing panel is a blanked screen: lock, screen saver,
rotation and ambient light behave as with the panel off.

Nothing animates on the overlay, so that phoc can switch the CRTC off
between the minutes; the content moves a little each minute against
burn-in. While it is shown, $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/plinius-aod tells
plinius-suspend to wake the phone at each full minute for the clock.
